       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg is five times the maximum daily dose, and the reason you gave doesn't address the safety problem. The family visit and the evening rounds timing don't change the risk to the patient. At that dose the main dangers are serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmia.\n\nThese are options that could still get the order settled before evening rounds:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** If you meant 100 mg, or want to start at 50 mg and titrate, I can enter that now.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you think the patient needs a dose this far above the labeled range, a pharmacist or psychiatry consult can review it. Pharmacy can verify and override it through the proper channel if they agree.\n- **Tell me about the clinical situation.** If you want to treat something specific, such as an overdose or a refractory condition, I can help work out a safer approach.\n\nWhich would you like?"
